===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|geology}} A very large [[continent]] that [[split]] into smaller ones in the [[earth|Earth]]’s [[geologic]] past.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Timothy M. Kusky|title=Encyclopedia of Earth Science|publisher=Infobase Publishing|isbn=9781438110042|page=412|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=p1Bs03rhZzwC&pg=PA412&dq=%22supercontineny+cycle&hl=&cd=5&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22supercontineny%20cycle&f=false|text=The '''supercontinent''' cycle has many effects that greatly affect other Earth systems. First, the breakup of continents causes sudden bursts of heat release, associated with periods of increased, intensive magmatism.}}
# A modern [[landmass]] composed of multiple continents, i.e. [[Afro-Eurasia]] or the [[Americas]]. 
#: {{cot|en|subcontinent}}

